Hey, I'm working on an embedded C++ project for an automotive ECU and I've hit a wall. We're seeing a slow memory leak that only manifests after about 4-6 hours of continuous operation. It's not crashing the system immediately, but the heap usage just keeps climbing until it hits the limit.

Here is a simplified version of the telemetry loop where I suspect the issue might be:

```cpp
void telemetry_task() {
    while (system_running) {
        SensorData* data = new SensorData();
        data->timestamp = get_timestamp();
        data->reading = read_sensor();

        if (data->reading > THRESHOLD) {
            LogEntry* entry = new LogEntry(data);
            event_queue.push(entry);
        }

        // potential issue area
        process_buffer(data); 

        sleep_ms(10);
    }
}
```

I've checked basic pointer assignments, but I can't find where the allocation isn't being freed. Can you give me a systematic approach to locating the specific leak in this kind of RTOS environment?

